Proof hooks suggested by this run
  1. Strong route: prove no four-tetrahedra defects occur beyond 343867.
     The computation matches the reported 241-defect frontier through 1,000,000.
  2. Weaker descent route: prove that for all large k there is no pair
     r, r+tri(k) in the four-defect set with 0 <= r < Te_{k+1}-Te_k,
     where tri(k)=Te_k-Te_{k-1}=k(k+1)/2 is the one-back gap.
     Then every shell is covered by Te_k or Te_{k-1} plus four atoms.
  3. Finite certificate route: the width-3 nearby-anchor stencil covers
     every sampled shell through k=1200, and width-1 covers after k=825.
